  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "T-state, machine cycle and instruction cycle"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The crystal frequency is divided by 2 inside the 8085: a 6 MHz crystal gives a 3 MHz operating clock. One clock period is a T-state ($T = 1/f$). A machine cycle is the time for one bus operation: opcode fetch (usually 4 T-states), memory read (3), memory write (3), I/O read (3) and I/O write (3). An instruction cycle is the time to fetch and execute one instruction and contains one or more machine cycles. The status lines S1 S0 identify the cycle: 11 opcode fetch, 10 read, 01 write, 00 halt."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "f(operating) = f(crystal)/2"
    },
    {
     "en": "T-state = 1/f"
    },
    {
     "en": "Opcode fetch 4T; memory/I/O read or write 3T"
    },
    {
     "en": "Instruction cycle = one or more machine cycles"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "One clock period is a T-state. A bus operation is a machine cycle, such as the four T-state opcode fetch, and an instruction cycle is made of one or more machine cycles.",
    "kn": "ಒಂದು ಕ್ಲಾಕ್ ಅವಧಿ ಒಂದು T-ಸ್ಥಿತಿ. ಒಂದು ಬಸ್ ಕಾರ್ಯ ಒಂದು ಯಂತ್ರ ಚಕ್ರ, ಉದಾ. 4 T-ಸ್ಥಿತಿಗಳ ಆಪ್‌ಕೋಡ್ ಫೆಚ್; ಸೂಚನಾ ಚಕ್ರ ಒಂದು ಅಥವಾ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಯಂತ್ರ ಚಕ್ರಗಳು."
   },
   "formula": "T = \\frac{1}{f}, \\qquad f = \\frac{f_{crystal}}{2}"
  },
